Chapter: Phase Allocator
  cites Codex chapter BootPaint (bp-rtc-seconds, bp-log-phase)

Section: Primitives

  pitch : Integer -> Integer
  pitch (size) =
   let p = __heap-save
   in let advanced = __heap-advance size
   in p

  strike : Integer -> Nothing
  strike (start) =
   __heap-restore start

 A deck reservation is ONE advance of the whole deck height, hundreds of
 megabytes, so it steps clean over the 2 MB guard page below the boot stack and
 the page never sees it. Measured 2026-08-04: the whole-compiler `-IrCce` run
 crossed the guard at 2974 MB and died at 3034 MB in a 75-byte `__str_concat`
 with the guard page present and silent. The page catches many small bumps; it
 structurally cannot catch one big one.

 So the big ones are checked here instead, which is affordable because this is
 the chokepoint the 58 inline bump sites do not have: one compare per deck,
 thirteen per compile, against one per allocation.

  guard-page-base-cell : Integer = 36320

  guard-page-plausible-floor : Integer = 1073741824

  build : Integer -> Integer
  build (size) =
   let p = __heap-save
   in let deck-init = __deck-set p
   in let guarded = deck-reservation-guard p size
   in let advanced = __heap-advance size
   in p

  deck-reservation-guard : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  deck-reservation-guard (p) (size) =
   let guard-base = peek-qword guard-page-base-cell 0
   in if guard-base >= guard-page-plausible-floor & p + size >= guard-base
      then poke-byte guard-base 0 0
      else 0

  seal : Integer -> Nothing
  seal (start) =
   __heap-advance 0

  deck-record : a -> a
  deck-record (x) =
   x

Section: Mountain Base

  init-phase-allocator : Integer
  init-phase-allocator =
   let base = __heap-save
   in let deck-init = __deck-set base
   in base

Section: Phase Measurement

  PhaseStart = record {
   bivy-origin : Integer,
   deck-origin : Integer,
   started : Integer
  }

  PhaseMetrics = record {
   label : Text,
   bivy-origin : Integer,
   bivy-hwm : Integer,
   deck-origin : Integer,
   deck-end : Integer
  }

  phase-start : PhaseStart
  phase-start =
   let bivy = pitch 0
   in PhaseStart { bivy-origin = bivy, deck-origin = __deck-pos, started = bp-rtc-seconds 0 }

 The log row is banked as the phase closes: label, wall seconds (RTC,
 armed-guarded, zero everywhere but a flight), and megabytes of bivy growth.
 bp-log-phase also advances the painted phase strip, which is what keeps a
 long silent phase legible on a board whose only channel is the glass.

  phase-took : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  phase-took (started) (now) =
   if now >= started then now - started else now - started + 86400

  phase-measure : PhaseStart, Text -> PhaseMetrics
  phase-measure (ps) (label) =
   let hwm = __heap-save
   in let deck-now = __deck-pos
   in let lg = bp-log-phase label (phase-took (ps.started) (bp-rtc-seconds 0)) ((hwm - (ps.bivy-origin)) / 1048576)
   in deck-record (PhaseMetrics {
    label = label,
    bivy-origin = ps.bivy-origin,
    bivy-hwm = hwm,
    deck-origin = ps.deck-origin,
    deck-end = deck-now
   })

  deck-short-of : Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  deck-short-of (ceiling) (band) =
   if ceiling > 0 & __deck-pos + band >= ceiling then True else False

 __deck-pos reads the deck-pos cell. deck-record is compiled by
 emit-deck-record-wrapper into __deck-enter, the body, __deck-exit:
 enter copies the cell into R10 and exit writes R10 back, and the
 write-back happens only when the nesting counter returns to zero. So
 inside a phase-wide deck-record extent the cell is FROZEN at the
 deck's base for the whole phase, and every allocation in that extent
 moves R10 instead. A loop that sits inside such an extent and asks
 deck-short-of is asking whether base + band >= base + height -- a
 question about the FLOOR's width that never mentions the usage, true
 only when the floor is narrower than the band.

 Measured 2026-07-21: an in-loop probe through rewrite-ir-defs, over
 the 2.81 MB selfhost, printed __deck-pos as 0x168961a2 on every one
 of its iterations while the phase wrote 19.1 MB. Starving that floor
 to 16 MB did not raise CDX9002; it crashed in __text_compare on a
 garbage pointer, which is the failure the guard exists to prevent,
 with the guard present and compiled in.

  deck-bound-short-of : Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  deck-bound-short-of (ceiling) (band) =
   if ceiling > 0 & __heap-save + band >= ceiling then True else False

  phase-compact : Nothing = __heap-restore (__deck-pos)

  phase-compact-poison : Integer -> Nothing
  phase-compact-poison (byte) =
   let old-top = __heap-save
   in let new-top = __deck-pos
   in let restored = __heap-restore new-top
   in if old-top > new-top then __memset new-top byte (old-top - new-top)
      else restored

